  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«Bao giờ»: position and context",
     "texto": [
      "**Bao giờ** at the beginning usually asks about a future moment: **Bao giờ chị Hoa đi Hạ Long?** = When will Hoa go to Hạ Long?",
      "At the end it usually asks when something happened, if the context indicates the past: **Anh David đi Việt Nam bao giờ?** = When did David go to Vietnam?",
      "It's a useful pattern, not an automatic rule: look at the context and time expressions too. **Khi nào** and **lúc nào** can appear in different positions."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "What has just happened and what is about to happen",
     "texto": [
      "**vừa / mới / vừa mới** + verb = to have just: **Tôi vừa mới về nhà.** = I've just got home.",
      "**sắp** + verb = to be about to: **Tôi sắp đi chợ.** = I'm about to go to the market.",
      "The order with the negation and «also»: **cũng + time marker + không + verb**: **Anh ấy cũng sẽ không đi.** = He won't go either."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Hurry: kẻo (or else…)",
     "texto": [
      "**kẻo** = or else, lest: **Chúng ta nhanh lên kẻo nhỡ tàu.** = Let's hurry up or we'll miss the train.",
      "Exclamations of panic: **Chết rồi!** = Oh my goodness! · **Nhanh lên!** = Hurry up!"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Office and shop opening hours",
     "texto": [
      "Opening hours vary depending on the organisation, city and type of shop. To understand the hours, look at the day, the opening time (**mở cửa**) and the closing time (**đóng cửa**).",
      "**cửa hàng bách hóa** = department store · **đại sứ quán** = embassy · **cơ quan** = office or organisation."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
